📅 Day 51 – Introduction to JSP (JavaServer Pages)

Full Stack Web Development with Java Internship

Today’s session focused on JSP (JavaServer Pages) and its role in developing dynamic web applications. The mentor explained how JSP simplifies server-side programming by allowing Java code to be embedded directly into HTML.

🔹 Topics Covered
1️⃣ Introduction to JSP
JSP is used to create dynamic web content
Allows embedding Java code within HTML
Easier to use compared to servlets for UI development
Runs on the server and generates HTML response
2️⃣ JSP Directives

JSP directives are used to control page configuration:

✅ page Directive
Defines page-level settings (language, import, etc.)
<%@ page language="java" %>
✅ include Directive
Includes content from another file
<%@ include file="header.jsp" %>
✅ taglib Directive
Used to include custom tag libraries (JSTL)
<%@ taglib uri="..." prefix="c" %>
